<title>BRAZIL: Brazil holds meeting on sugar crop plan.</title>
<headline>Brazil holds meeting on sugar crop plan.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian government officials and private sector producers were holding a regular meeting Thursday to discuss the 1997/98 sugar crop plan, a Ministry of Industry and Commerce spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the meeting was being attended by the head of the ministry's sugar and alcohol department, Pedro Cabral. Mauricio Assis, head of the primary commodities department, was travelling, she said.</p>
<p>The sugar crop plan, which has traditionally set a limit for exports, is expected to be ready by May.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
